\section*{Classification of semialgebraic projective universal covers}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
A normal projective universal cover is claimed to have a semialgebraic projective model exactly when it decomposes into a symmetric bounded-domain factor, a complex affine-space factor, and a simply connected normal projective factor. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Mathematical claim 1.} For any connected normal projective complex variety $X$, OpenAI claims equivalence between its ordinary universal cover being biholomorphic to an open semialgebraic subset in some projective variety and a decomposition
\[
\widetilde X\simeq D\times\mathbb C^m\times F,
\]
where $m\ge0$, $D$ is a bounded symmetric domain, while $F$ is projective, normal and simply connected; either may be a point. Semialgebraic means finite Boolean operations on real-polynomial equality or inequality conditions in an algebraic presentation. No algebraicity of deck transformations is assumed. The projection to $D\times\mathbb C^m$ is claimed to be the Remmert reduction, proper with connected compact fibers and unchanged holomorphic function sheaf; thus the cover is holomorphically convex and is Stein exactly when $F$ is a point.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 058, 2026-09-24): Boundary windows produce compact projective fibers, and bounded plurisubharmonic parameter traces show that intersecting fibers coincide. Functions controlling moving chart boundaries globalize the quotient; inverse-chart compactness makes it a biholomorphism, and special-manifold abelianity controls the remaining deck action.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Manuscript 1 (family 058, 2026-09-24): The problem selects the mathematical statement summarized here, including its stated hypotheses and parameter range. The cited theorem gives a claimed proof of that assertion in full.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For family 058, the scope page documents the following selections. The selected bounded-domain result allows a singular affine ambient set and nonfree proper cocompact group action, and concludes smoothness and symmetry. It does not select the entire projective universal-cover classification. Manuscript 1 is not among the papers selected by that page, so the family link does not formalize its main conclusion.

This site has not executed the Lean files or checked their dependencies. These descriptions report the scope of the linked declarations, rather than a new verification of the proofs.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these results to an internal model. Its release notice cautions that results lacking full formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently assessed the proofs; a solved label records the scope of the reported claim.

